  "body": "### Description\nThe `init()` function in the `BuilderWallet` contract lacks any access control checks. This allows any arbitrary user to call the function and overwrite the `builderAdmin` address repeatedly.\n\nhttps://github.com/code-423n4/2025-12-panoptic/blob/fe557748210a529ae414d7c487b6514be0d9e220/contracts/RiskEngine.sol#L2315-L2317\n\n```solidity\n    function init(address _builderAdmin) external {\n        builderAdmin = _builderAdmin;\n    }\n```\n\n An attacker can take over the `builderAdmin` role and use the `sweep()` function to drain all tokens from the `BuilderWallet`.\n\n```solidity\n    function sweep(address token, address to) external {\n        if (msg.sender != builderAdmin) revert Errors.NotBuilder();\n\n\n        uint256 bal = IERC20(token).balanceOf(address(this));\n        if (bal == 0) return;\n\n\n        bool ok = IERC20(token).transfer(to, bal);\n        if (!ok) {\n            // `from` is this wallet, `balance` is pre-transfer token balance\n            revert Errors.TransferFailed(token, address(this), bal, bal);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n```\n\n## Impact\n\nLoss of Funds.\n\n## Mitigate \nAdd access control và initialization check\n```solidity\nfunction init(address _builderAdmin) external {  \n    require(msg.sender == FACTORY, \"Only factory can initialize\");  \n    require(builderAdmin == address(0), \"Already initialized\");  \n    builderAdmin = _builderAdmin;  \n}\n```",
